From c60c926c4e3e73500b4599f6f1c276b0b4befe88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:35:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] branding: FlyWeb icons for Linux (window, launcher,
 installer)

The Linux icons were still Brave's lion: app/theme/brave/linux/
product_logo_{24,48,64,128,256}.png, the 128 channel variants, the
installer's product_logo_32.xpm and
default_100_percent/brave/linux/product_logo_{16,32,32_*}.png
(IDR_PRODUCT_LOGO_32_* and the 128 BINDATA used for the window icon).

They are now the same images as their macOS/common counterparts,
rendered from the same masters by FlyWeb/branding/scripts/
generar-marca.sh (M1-01 for the app icon, O1-01 for the development
channel, M2 for 16/32). The XPM is made from the 32 px PNG with
png2xpm.py. Nothing for macOS changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MwmK2hjxRPyuefYzGRoZRk
